<p>Hi. Thank you for your thoughts, I've taken them all on board.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Very strange that only O5 council members can access the SCP's containment<br />
seeing how they generally aren't supposed to come in contact with anomalies.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>In my mind, the O5 council members <em>wouldn't</em> be coming into contact with the object, only very select staff. I wrote it in accordance with what is stated in the Guide Hub:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>Level 5 security clearances are given to the highest-ranking administrative<br />
personnel within the Foundation and grant effectively unlimited access to all<br />
strategic and otherwise sensitive data. Level 5 security clearances are typically<br />
only granted to O5 Council members <strong>and selected staff</strong>.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>This sentence doesn't make sense to me. Is it a crystal with a<br />
cognitohazardous effect, because this sentence seems to imply that the<br />
crystal itself is like the physical embodiment of the cognitohazard or something?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sorry if it wasn't clear. What I meant it to mean was that the crystal is a cognitohazard if you touch it, thereby a &quot;tactile cognitohazard&quot; (although it was eventually discovered physical touch isn't necessary, which is why it was struck through.)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The description is simply put, painful to get through. I'd say you could cut<br />
at least half of those words out and it'd still make just as much sense. There<br />
is no hook; some kind of mystery in the conprocs to pull you through all of that.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Noted; I'll try to be more succinct in future. The hook was supposed to be &quot;I wonder what these people are seeing after they die? Why won't they talk about it?&quot; Unfortunately, it doesn't look like it was that interesting, or I just didn't write it in an interesting way, or the concept itself is just inherently boring.</p>
<p>Anyway, thanks for all your feedback. Hopefully I'll do better next time!</p>

							</div>

								
