			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824758">
									

<p>I ultimately came down to a no-vote (neutral vote) on this.</p>
<p>I think the main problem here is that the core concept leans heavily on a few site cliches, and doesn't do enough to build beyond that. As a fan of technical scips, the tight tone and some interesting nuances to the effect helped sell me a bit on the idea (the experiment logs in particular have some good moments of black humor and creepiness), but ultimately there's no moment where I find myself saying &quot;oh?&#8230;ooohh&#8230;&quot; or staring at the screen processing the full ramifications of what I just read.</p>
<p>I'm not saying this can't work, but it might be one to put on the back-burner while you work on something more off the beaten trail; some of the best twists come from letting an idea sit for a while until you get one of those &quot;Oh duh, that's what I should do!&quot; moments.</p>

